# Privacy Policy for Lumen Lake

**Effective Date: October 12, 2026**

Thank you for playing Lumen Lake.

Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how information may be collected and used when you use the Lumen Lake mobile application.

## 1. Information We Collect

Lumen Lake does not require you to create an account, and we do not ask you for information such as your email address, phone number or postal address.

Lumen Lake uses third-party advertising services, including Google AdMob. These services may automatically collect certain information from your device in order to provide advertisements, measure their performance, prevent fraud, and maintain the advertising service.

Depending on your device, settings, location, and consent choices, this information may include:

* IP address
* Device and advertising identifiers
* General device information
* App interactions, such as app launches, taps, and ad interactions
* Diagnostic and performance information
* Approximate location derived from information such as your IP address

We do not directly receive information that identifies you personally from Google AdMob.

If you choose to sign in with Google Play Games, Lumen Lake also takes part in the World Scores leaderboards. The information this involves is described in section 3.

The game's music and sounds are included with the app. Lumen Lake does not use your device's microphone, camera, contacts or location services.

## 2. Information Stored on Your Device

Lumen Lake keeps a record of your play so that your progress, high scores, awards and settings are there the next time you play. This includes:

* The levels of the journey you have solved and the stars each earned, and the last level you played
* Your pearls, the game's own currency, which are earned by playing and can't be bought
* Your daily gift: the last day you collected it and how many days in a row you have
* Your high scores: the ten best Lantern Rushes, each with its score, the boards it solved, the day it was played and, if you were signed in to Google Play Games, your Play Games name
* The awards you have won and when each was won
* Running totals of your play that awards are won by, such as the boards you have solved, the hints you have used, the pearls you have earned, the rushes you have played, the days you have played and your total play time, together with the last day you played
* Your sound volumes and your display settings, such as grid brightness, stream corners and camera angle
* While you are signed in to Google Play Games, your best Lantern Rush score until it has been sent to the World Scores (see section 3)

This information is stored on your own device. Apart from what section 3 describes, it is not transmitted to us or to any third party, and we have no access to it. If your device backs up its apps' data (on Android, to your Google account), it may include this information in that backup, which is kept by your device's provider, not by us.

You can erase your progress, pearls, daily gift, high scores and awards at any time using the START AGAIN FROM NOTHING control on the app's settings screen. Your sound volumes and display settings are kept until you change them. That control does not remove your World Scores entries; section 3 explains how to remove those. Uninstalling the app erases everything stored on your device.

## 3. World Scores

World Scores are online leaderboards where Lantern Rush scores are compared with other players, worldwide and in your own country, for all time, this month, this week and today. Taking part is optional: you take part only if you sign in with Google Play Games.

While you are signed in, Lumen Lake sends your best Lantern Rush scores to the World Scores after each rush. For each entry it sends:

* Your Google Play Games display name
* Your score and the number of boards you solved
* Your country, as a two-letter code
* Your device's platform (Android or iOS)
* A user identifier created for the app by Google Firebase Authentication
* The date and time the entry was saved

Your country is taken from your SIM card, or else from the mobile network you are connected to, or else from your device's language and region settings. Lumen Lake does not use GPS or your device's location services to find it.

Other players of Lumen Lake can see the World Scores. Each entry is shown with its rank, your Play Games name, your score, the boards you solved and your country's flag.

Only your best score for each leaderboard is kept, and it replaces your previous one when you beat it.

The World Scores are stored with Google Firebase (Cloud Firestore and Firebase Authentication), which Google operates on our behalf. We use them only to run the leaderboards and do not sell or share them for any other purpose.

### Deleting your World Scores account

You can delete your World Scores account at any time using the DELETE MY WORLD SCORES ACCOUNT control on the app's settings screen. This deletes all of your World Scores entries and the user identifier Firebase Authentication created for you, and signs you out of the World Scores. Lumen Lake then sends nothing more until you choose to sign in again on the scores screen, which starts a new account.

You can also ask us to delete your World Scores account and entries without using the app: email [axiomaragames@gmail.com](mailto:axiomaragames@gmail.com) with the subject "Delete my Lumen Lake account" and the Google Play Games name shown on your entries. We delete them within 30 days and confirm by email. Nothing is kept after deletion.

You can also disconnect Lumen Lake from your Google account in your Google Play Games or Google account settings.

## 4. Advertising

Lumen Lake is supported by advertisements provided through Google AdMob.

The app shows banner advertisements on its menu and on its levels, scores, awards and settings screens. No banner is shown while you play.

The app also offers optional rewarded video advertisements. Watching one to the end can double the pearls a level or a rush earned, triple your daily gift, give you a hint, undo or restart when you don't have enough pearls, or collect the awards a game earned you. Watching a rewarded video is always your choice. If you decline, you simply don't get that reward. For awards, this means the awards from that game are not collected, but they can be earned again.

Depending on your location, device settings, and consent choices, advertisements may be personalized or non-personalized.

Google and its advertising partners may use device identifiers and other information to provide, measure, personalize, and improve advertising and to detect and prevent fraud.

For more information about how Google uses information from apps that use its services, please see Google's privacy information:

https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

## 5. Internet Access

Lumen Lake can be played without an internet connection. Advertisements, rewarded videos and the World Scores need one. While your device is offline, rewarded videos are unavailable and the World Scores wait until you are back online.

The app does not check your connection separately. It only notices that it is offline when an advertisement or a World Scores request cannot reach the internet. It does not look at which network you are connected to.

## 6. Consent and Privacy Choices

Where required by applicable law, users may be presented with a consent message that allows them to make choices regarding the use of their information for advertising purposes.

Where such a choice has been presented, it can be revisited at any time using the PRIVACY OPTIONS control on the app's settings screen.

Users may also be able to control advertising personalization and advertising identifiers through their device privacy settings.

## 7. Children's Privacy

Lumen Lake is a general-audience game.

We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children.

Advertising services used by the app may process information as described in this Privacy Policy. Where required, appropriate restrictions are applied to advertising and data processing.

Parents or guardians who have questions regarding their child's privacy may contact us using the email address provided below.

## 8. Data Security

We do not operate our own servers. The World Scores are kept with Google Firebase, and only the player who saved an entry can change or remove it.

Information processed by third-party services such as Google AdMob, Google Play Games and Google Firebase is handled according to their respective privacy and security practices.

Information sent by the app to these services is encrypted in transit.

## 9. Third-Party Services

Lumen Lake uses third-party services that may collect or process information according to their own privacy policies:

**Google AdMob**: advertising, including rewarded video advertising, advertising measurement, analytics related to advertising, and fraud prevention. Its consent message is provided by Google's User Messaging Platform.

**Google Play Games Services**: the optional sign-in and the Play Games name used for the World Scores.

**Google Firebase (Authentication and Cloud Firestore)**: the World Scores leaderboards.

